A clause splits on its first `=` only: everything after it is the value, so a frontmatter
value that itself carries an `=` is addressable.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: Alpha
k: a=b
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/beta/index.md --
---
title: Beta
k: a
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where 'k=a=b' --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/alpha/index.md
-- stderr --
